WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.698
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:05.998 --> 00:00:09.478
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.778 --> 00:00:16.076
Unit seven: Paragraph Writing. Today you will write a clear paragraph with a topic sentence and support.

4
00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:19.051
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.465
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.329
Paragraph.

7
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.524
Paragraph means a group of sentences about one idea.

8
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:31.582
Write one paragraph.

9
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:34.824
Your turn. Say: Paragraph.

10
00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:38.726
Paragraph.

11
00:00:39.483 --> 00:00:40.473
Unity.

12
00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:43.622
Unity means having one main idea.

13
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.042
A paragraph needs unity.

14
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.070
Your turn. Say: Unity.

15
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:52.737
Unity.

16
00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:54.693
Coherence.

17
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:58.519
Coherence means clear connection between ideas.

18
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:01.023
Use linkers for coherence.

19
00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:04.083
Your turn. Say: Coherence.

20
00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:07.958
Coherence.

21
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:09.636
Concluding.

22
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.557
Concluding means ending a text.

23
00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:14.906
Add a concluding sentence.

24
00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:18.099
Your turn. Say: Concluding.

25
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:21.876
Concluding.

26
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:23.513
Relevant.

27
00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.806
Relevant means connected to the topic.

28
00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:29.080
Use relevant examples.

29
00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:32.208
Your turn. Say: Relevant.

30
00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:36.045
Relevant.

31
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:37.842
Elaborate.

32
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.128
Elaborate means to give more detail.

33
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:43.426
Elaborate on your idea.

34
00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:46.634
Your turn. Say: Elaborate.

35
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.687
Elaborate.

36
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.451
Sequence.

37
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.635
Sequence means the order of ideas.

38
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.913
Keep a logical sequence.

39
00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:01.273
Your turn. Say: Sequence.

40
00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.332
Sequence.

41
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:07.061
Cohesive.

42
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.282
Cohesive means sticking together well.

43
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:12.744
Write a cohesive text.

44
00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.909
Your turn. Say: Cohesive.

45
00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:19.605
Cohesive.

46
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.062
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:26.963
Visal, what makes a good paragraph?

48
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:38.342
It has one main idea. Start with a topic sentence, add two or three supporting sentences with examples and end with a concluding sentence.

49
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.055
What is coherence?

50
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:51.313
Coherence means the ideas follow a logical order and are connected with linkers such as first, however and as a result.

51
00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:54.312
How long should a paragraph be?

52
00:02:55.417 --> 00:03:04.559
Usually five to eight sentences. If it becomes much longer, check whether you have two ideas and split it into two paragraphs.

53
00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.224
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:12.219
Grammar focus: Topic sentence, support and conclusion.

55
00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:13.683
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:20.394
Reading improves vocabulary. For example, readers meet new words. Therefore, read daily.

57
00:03:21.283 --> 00:03:27.038
Exercise helps students. It reduces stress. So, exercise often.

58
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:34.783
Start with a topic sentence, support it with examples and finish with a concluding sentence that repeats the idea in new words.

59
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:39.643
Be careful! Don't say: Each paragraph have two ideas.

60
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.319
Say: Each paragraph has one idea.

61
00:03:44.619 --> 00:03:46.375
Has after a singular noun.

62
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.877
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:51.819
My Paragraph.

64
00:03:52.119 --> 00:03:54.339
Rina writes a paragraph about reading.

65
00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:58.540
Her topic sentence says that reading improves vocabulary.

66
00:03:59.533 --> 00:04:02.891
She adds an example about meeting new words in context.

67
00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.805
She links her ideas with first and as a result.

68
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.053
Her last sentence advises students to read every day.

69
00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:16.354
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:17.217 --> 00:04:19.390
A paragraph has one blank idea.

71
00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.438
A, hidden. B, main. C, hundred.

72
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.988
The answer is B: main.

73
00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.382
The first sentence is the blank sentence.

74
00:04:31.682 --> 00:04:34.906
A, last. B, free. C, topic.

75
00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.188
The answer is C: topic.

76
00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:42.966
Linkers help blank.

77
00:04:43.266 --> 00:04:47.175
A, coherence. B, noise. C, speed.

78
00:04:50.733 --> 00:04:53.058
The answer is A: coherence.

79
00:04:54.217 --> 00:04:56.565
A concluding sentence blank the paragraph.

80
00:04:56.865 --> 00:05:00.483
A, skips. B, ends. C, starts.

81
00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.986
The answer is B: ends.

82
00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.708
What does Rina advise?

83
00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:12.824
A, stop reading. B, sleep more. C, read daily.

84
00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.413
The answer is C: read daily.

85
00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.612
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:25.078
What makes a good paragraph?

87
00:05:33.883 --> 00:05:35.360
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:49.415
A good paragraph has one main idea. It starts with a topic sentence, gives examples as support and ends with a concluding sentence. I use linkers so the ideas connect clearly.

89
00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:51.424
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:52.317 --> 00:05:57.303
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and topic sentence, support and conclusion.

91
00:05:57.603 --> 00:06:03.575
Today's value is organizational clarity. Make sure everyone knows their role and responsibilities.

92
00:06:03.875 --> 00:06:06.388
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

93
00:06:06.688 --> 00:06:09.445
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

